WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.830
[Caller] Hey Rob, Jeff calling
from Northern Virginia.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.660
You've recommended other fantastic books.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.680
Would really like to know,
what else you recommend?

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.100
Or can you come out
with a list on your show

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.680
of Rob Lowe must reads or your top 20?

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.170
I really look forward to that.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:27.930
And again, just, I cannot tell
you what an experience I had

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:28.970
with "The Moon's a Balloon."

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.630
Thank you so much for everything.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.740
Well, Jeff from Northern Virginia,

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.460
by the way, I love that
you're from Northern Virginia.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.903
It's like you're in a civil
war battalion, I love that.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.595
I'm from Northern Virginia.

00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:42.970
That's great.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.570
Thank you. I'm glad you
liked "The Moon's a Balloon."

00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:50.853
It was my inspiration
for writing my two books.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:55.370
So the Northern Virginia Civil War thing

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:58.350
made me think of one of my favorite books,

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:01.040
which is called "The Killer Angels."

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.100
And it is a book I believe
it won the Pulitzer Prize

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.320
and it is sort of the definitive account

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.620
of the Battle of Gettysburg.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.240
And you don't have to be a historian

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.440
or a Civil War buff to
read it, nor should you be.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.743
It's just the most beautifully
written, emotional,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.100
very short books I've ever read.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.713
So that's "The Killer Angels."

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.163
Another one I am loving is,

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.800
I believe it's called
"Under the Comanche Moon."

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.490
And I just heard that
Paul Thomas Anderson,

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.680
one of my favorite directors

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.080
has been secretly working
on the movie adaptation

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.120
of "Under a Comanche Moon."

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.640
So that is gonna be one of
the great movies of all time.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.540
And there you have it. Thanks.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.373
I love that.

00:01:52.373 --> 00:01:53.780
I need to do like an Oprah's book

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.250
like recommendation thing.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:57.010
Oprah, I'm coming for ya!

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.390
This is just the first version of it.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:01:59.940
Look out, there's more to come.

